IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- LAYER 1: OTHER MATTERS (sections 66 to 79).
--
-- What this part contains: section 68 (offences on the water within the Admiralty's
-- jurisdiction are punished as on land), section 76 (procedure for summary offences,
-- by reference to other Acts that are not inputs here) and section 78 (the Act does not
-- extend to Scotland).  Sections 66, 69 to 74, 77 and 79 are rows of dots; the text has
-- no row for section 67 or 75.

§ `Other Matters`

§§ `Section 66: blank in this text`

-- src:111 | 66 . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 66 (src:111)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 66: blank in this text` MEANS
    "Section 66 shows only its number and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode."

§§ `Section 68: offences committed within the jurisdiction of the Admiralty`

-- src:112 | 68 Offences committed within the jurisdiction of the Admiralty.
-- src:113 | All indictable offences mentioned in this Act which shall be committed within the jurisdiction of the Admiralty of England or Ireland shall be . . . liable to the same punishments, as if they had been committed upon the land in England or Ireland, . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 68 (src:112-113)
-- "All indictable offences mentioned in this Act which shall be committed within the
-- jurisdiction of the Admiralty of England or Ireland shall be . . . liable to the same
-- punishments, as if they had been committed upon the land in England or Ireland".
-- The text calls an offence "indictable" in two sections (16: "on indictment"; 47: "upon
-- an indictment") and says "before two justices of the peace" in three (39, 40, 42).
-- For the rest it does not say, so the encoding takes the mode of trial the text gives
-- and, where the text gives none, the person's statement that the offence is indictable.
DECLARE `Offence within the Admiralty jurisdiction` HAS
    `the offence is one mentioned in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how the text says the offence is tried` IS A `Mode of trial`
    `the offence is indictable, where the text does not say` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was committed within the jurisdiction of the Admiralty of England or Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 68 (src:113)
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence within the Admiralty jurisdiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68: the offence is indictable` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o's `how the text says the offence is tried`
    WHEN `on indictment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `summarily before justices of the peace` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text does not say` THEN o's `the offence is indictable, where the text does not say`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 68 (src:113)
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence within the Admiralty jurisdiction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68: the person is liable to the same punishments as if the offence had been committed upon the land` o MEANS
        o's `the offence is one mentioned in this Act`
    AND `s 68: the offence is indictable` o
    AND o's `it was committed within the jurisdiction of the Admiralty of England or Ireland`

