§§ `Section 78: Act not to extend to Scotland`

-- src:123 | 78 Act not to extend to Scotland.
-- src:124 | Nothing in this Act contained shall extend to Scotland, except as herein-before otherwise expressly provided.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 78 (src:123-124)
-- "Nothing in this Act contained shall extend to Scotland, except as herein-before
-- otherwise expressly provided."  This is the LAW'S OWN answer, not the encoder's: the
-- Act does not extend to Scotland unless an earlier provision expressly says it does.
-- In the deposited text no provision before section 78 names Scotland (a search of the
-- text finds the word only in section 78 itself); but the text carries ". . ." marks
-- where words were repealed, and those marks could be hiding such a provision, so the
-- fact is taken as an input, not assumed.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 78 (src:124)
GIVEN `a provision before section 78 expressly provides that the Act extends to Scotland for this matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78: the Act extends to Scotland for this matter` `a provision before section 78 expressly provides that the Act extends to Scotland for this matter` MEANS
    `a provision before section 78 expressly provides that the Act extends to Scotland for this matter`

